  "slug": "alignment-ohmic-controlled-selection-551c",
  "summary": "Foundation models and virtual knock-out tools are now tested against ClinVar, DepMap and single-cell data, exposing limits of current benchmarks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how well predictive models of genetic and transcriptional effects can be evaluated and trusted. Zero-shot virtual knock-out tools (scTenifoldKnk, CellOracle, Geneformer) tested on single-cell and DepMap data produce rankings that mostly reflect network topology rather than causal genes. In variant interpretation, six genomic foundation models benchmarked on 6,960 ClinVar variants in LGMD genes favor Evo2 with 501 bp context, although clinical utility remains untested. A Manski-bounds analysis shows that many pairwise comparisons of variant effect predictors are undecided because of unscored variants, motivating reach-aware reporting. SpliceVarMech adds a causal generative, Bayesian framework aimed at mechanistic interpretation of non-canonical splicing variants, benchmarked on male infertility genes and BRCA1. What is new is the emphasis on causal validity and variant coverage, rather than headline accuracy alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
